Deployment in IOS and adroid
----------------------------
Android (Google Play Store)
Step 1: Create a Google Play Developer Account
Go to the Google Play Console.
Create a Developer Account.
Pay the one-time registration fee.
Step 2: Change App Information

Update:

App Name
Package Name (cannot be changed after publishing)
App Icon
Splash Screen
Version Number

Example:

version: 1.0.0+1
Step 3: Create a Keystore

Generate the keystore:

keytool -genkeypair -v \
-keystore upload-keystore.jks \
-keyalg RSA \
-keysize 2048 \
-validity 10000 \
-alias upload
Step 4: Configure Signing
Create key.properties
Configure signing in Gradle
Add the .jks file
Step 5: Build the App
flutter clean
flutter pub get
flutter build appbundle

Generated file:

build/app/outputs/bundle/release/app-release.aab
Step 6: Create an App in Google Play Console

Fill in:

App Name
Default Language
App Category
Free or Paid
Step 7: Upload the AAB

Go to:

Production
      ↓
Create Release
      ↓
Upload app-release.aab
Step 8: Complete Store Listing

Add:

App Name
Short Description
Full Description
App Icon
Feature Graphic
Screenshots
Contact Email
Privacy Policy URL
Step 9: Fill Required Forms

Examples:

Data Safety
App Access
Ads Declaration
Content Rating
Target Audience
Step 10: Publish

Click:

Review Release
      ↓
Start Rollout to Production

Google reviews the app.

Usually:

1–7 days

Then it appears on the Play Store.

Android Deployment Flow
Flutter App
      ↓
Generate Keystore
      ↓
Configure Signing
      ↓
flutter build appbundle
      ↓
Upload AAB
      ↓
Complete Store Listing
      ↓
