iOS (Apple App Store)
Step 1: Apple Developer Account

Create an Apple Developer account.

This requires an annual subscription.

Step 2: Open the Flutter Project in Xcode
ios/

Open:

Runner.xcworkspace
Step 3: Configure Signing

In Xcode:

Runner
     ↓
Signing & Capabilities

Choose:

Apple Team
Bundle Identifier
Step 4: Set Version

Example:

version: 1.0.0+1
Step 5: Build iOS Release
flutter build ios --release

or

flutter build ipa
Step 6: Archive the App

In Xcode:

Product
      ↓
Archive
Step 7: Upload to App Store Connect

Use:

Organizer
      ↓
Distribute App
      ↓
Upload
Step 8: Create App Store Listing

Add:

App Name
Description
Keywords
Screenshots
Privacy Policy
Support URL
Step 9: Submit for Review

Apple reviews the app.

Usually:

1–3 days

Sometimes longer.

Step 10: Release

After approval:

Release

Your app appears on the App Store.

